    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d27">

                <pb facs="0114" n="40" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg40"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1644.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>, </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-12-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 30, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    despatch of the 14th instant, No. 1110, and in reply to inform you that the
                    Secretary of the Navy, to whom it was referred, states that his department has
                    not the officers or men to spare for the purpose of bringing to a port of the
                    United States the Shenandoah, but that whenever that vessel reaches one of our
                    ports through other means, the Navy Department will, if requested, be happy to
                    take charge of her.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d27-a1.xml" xpointer="d27-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
